/*!
    \page kwi-terminal-hello-world.html
    \title Hello World
    \brief A minimal terminal window in QML.

    This example opens an interactive shell in a window with a scrollbar.
    Save it as \c Main.qml:

    \qml
    import QtQuick
    import org.kde.kwi.terminal

    Window {
        width: 800
        height: 500
        visible: true
        title: "Hello World"

        Session {
            id: shell
            onExited: Qt.quit()
        }

        Terminal {
            anchors.fill: parent
            session: shell
            focus: true
        }

        Component.onCompleted: shell.start()
    }
    \endqml

    \l Session owns the process and terminal contents. Leaving
    \l {Session::executable}{executable} unset selects the user's default shell.
    The call to \l {Session::start()}{start()} launches it once the component is ready.

    \l Terminal displays the session and provides the scrollbar. Setting
    \l {Item::focus}{focus} lets it accept keyboard input. When the shell exits,
    the \l {Session::exited()}{onExited} handler closes the application.

    With the module and its dependencies installed in your QML import path,
    run the file with Qt's \c qml tool:

    \badcode
    qml Main.qml
    \endcode

    Type a command to use the terminal, or enter \c exit to close the window.

    \sa {Kwi Terminal QML Types}
*/
